      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first summer resort in Adams County, York Sulphur Springs drew visitors from Philadelphia and Baltimore by stage coach in the early 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York_Springs%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "General George Washington and his wife Martha spent a summer in 1799 at the springs, a visit that put the town on the map.",
